  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Assistance with Emergency Shelter and Household Items and Site Management for Displaced Populations in North Kivu</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In response to the ongoing humanitarian crisis in eastern Democratic Republic of the Congo, particularly the acute needs among displaced populations in North Kivu, the International Organization for Migration (IOM) is providing emergency assistance in the form of shelter/non-food items and camp coordination and camp management to reinforce the dignity of displaced persons and reduce reliance on negative coping mechanisms. The assistance ultimately restores access to decent shelter, non-food items and income-generating activities, specifically in the form of providing light shelter kits and strengthening camp coordination and management at eight sites under IOM management in North Kivu.</narrative>
  </description>
